    title: "Iran vows to use 'all avaliable tools' to confront US naval blockade",
    summary: "Iran vows to use 'all avaliable tools' to confront US naval blockade Iran has warned the US against its naval blockade of Iranian oil exports, with Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei saying Tehran would not tolerate the \"American aggression\". “We will use all the means at our disposal to counter US aggression,” Baqaei said on Monday. The blockade, first imposed in April and halted in June, was reinstated in July after a memorandum of understanding between Washington and Tehran collapsed. This warning comes as the two countries continue to exchange accusations over attacks in the Gulf. Bahrain said an Iranian attack hit a civilian industrial facility on Saturday, while the Iranian Revolutionary Guard Corps said they had launched missiles and drones on US ‌military positions in the country. Iran has warned the US against its naval blockade of Iranian oil exports, with Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei saying Iran would not tolerate the \"American aggression\". https://t.co/r42wEC4YPH — Middle East Eye (@MiddleEastEye) November 23, 2026",
    preview: "Iran vows to use 'all avaliable tools' to confront US naval blockade Iran has warned the US against its naval blockade of Iranian oil exports, with Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei saying Tehran would not tolerate the \"American aggression\". “We will use all the means at our disposal to counter US aggression,” Baqaei said on Monday. The blockade, first imposed in April and halted in June, was reinstated in July after a memorandum of understanding between Washington and Tehran collapsed.",
    body: "Iran vows to use 'all avaliable tools' to confront US naval blockade Iran has warned the US against its naval blockade of Iranian oil exports, with Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei saying Tehran would not tolerate the \"American aggression\". “We will use all the means at our disposal to counter US aggression,” Baqaei said on Monday. The blockade, first imposed in April and halted in June, was reinstated in July after a memorandum of understanding between Washington and Tehran collapsed.\n\nThis warning comes as the two countries continue to exchange accusations over attacks in the Gulf. Bahrain said an Iranian attack hit a civilian industrial facility on Saturday, while the Iranian Revolutionary Guard Corps said they had launched missiles and drones on US ‌military positions in the country. Iran has warned the US against its naval blockade of Iranian oil exports, with Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei saying Iran would not tolerate the \"American aggression\".\n\nhttps://t.co/r42wEC4YPH — Middle East Eye (@MiddleEastEye) November 23, 2026",
