    title: "Crucial draw sets up decisive Morocco–Spain showdown",
    summary: "Morocco battled back from two goals down to snatch a crucial late draw against China, keeping their hopes of reaching the next round alive ahead of a decisive clash with Group H leaders Spain.",
    preview: "Morocco Morocco battled back from two goals down to snatch a crucial late draw against China, keeping their hopes of reaching the next round alive ahead of a decisive clash with Group H leaders Spain. Coach Ahmed Kantari praised his players’ resilience: “I would like to congratulate the players for their character because they stayed focused until the end.",
    body: "Morocco\n\nMorocco battled back from two goals down to snatch a crucial late draw against China, keeping their hopes of reaching the next round alive ahead of a decisive clash with Group H leaders Spain.\n\nCoach Ahmed Kantari praised his players’ resilience: “I would like to congratulate the players for their character because they stayed focused until the end. It’s never easy to concede a goal so early, but we stayed focused until the last minute, and we deserved this draw.”\n\nA Moroccan player also thanked the supporters for their backing, saying: “Many people love football, and they helped us perform. We thank them.”\n\nMorocco now need at least a draw against Spain to secure their place in the next round of 32.",
