    title: "Ukraine strike on Russian warship off Libya highlights Kyiv’s broadened reach",
    summary: "Kyiv's security service said the drones used in the attack were transported to an undisclosed location and launched from a mothership.",
    preview: "Ukraine claimed responsibility for sinking a Russian warship and another sanctioned vessel off the coast of Libya in what President Volodymyr Zelenskyy called an exemplary operation in response to Moscow’s war. Seven Ukrainian-made sea drones struck a Russian military corvette Merkury docked at Benghazi’s naval base early on Sunday, Zelenskyy wrote in a social media post. Kyiv’s forces also destroyed a Russian Ka-27 combat helicopter and hit a dry cargo vessel MV ANGARA, which Moscow used to transport weapons, the president said on Monday.",
    body: "Ukraine claimed responsibility for sinking a Russian warship and another sanctioned vessel off the coast of Libya in what President Volodymyr Zelenskyy called an exemplary operation in response to Moscow’s war.\n\nSeven Ukrainian-made sea drones struck a Russian military corvette Merkury docked at Benghazi’s naval base early on Sunday, Zelenskyy wrote in a social media post. Kyiv’s forces also destroyed a Russian Ka-27 combat helicopter and hit a dry cargo vessel MV ANGARA, which Moscow used to transport weapons, the president said on Monday.\n\nUkraine has been expanding its strikes on Russian shipping, especially in the Black Sea, as it seeks to undercut the Kremlin’s ability to finance its war from oil sales. But the latest attacks significantly broaden Kyiv’s reach by affecting Moscow’s activities in North Africa.",
