    title: "U.N. food agency chief warns wars jeopardize food aid for 7.3 million more people",
    summary: "The agency head has said that war-related shipping chokepoints and climate shocks like El Nino are compounding food insecurity challenges.",
    preview: "World Food Program (WFP) Executive Director Luke Lindberg warned on Monday that shipping chokepoints linked to wars in the Middle East and Ukraine could raise the agency’s costs by $727 million by mid-2027, threatening food aid for 7.3 million more people. Lindberg, whom U.S. President Donald Trump nominated and the United Nations appointed in September to head the world’s largest humanitarian agency, called for new efforts to safeguard humanitarian shipments of Ukrainian and Russian grain through the Black Sea, modeled on a U.N.-brokered initiative…",
    body: "World Food Program (WFP) Executive Director Luke Lindberg warned on Monday that shipping chokepoints linked to wars in the Middle East and Ukraine could raise the agency’s costs by $727 million by mid-2027, threatening food aid for 7.3 million more people.\n\nLindberg, whom U.S. President Donald Trump nominated and the United Nations appointed in September to head the world’s largest humanitarian agency, called for new efforts to safeguard humanitarian shipments of Ukrainian and Russian grain through the Black Sea, modeled on a U.N.-brokered initiative that was in effect from 2022 to 2023.\n\nLindberg told the U.N. Security Council that constraints on food exports and farming inputs passing through the Strait of Hormuz, the Bab el-Mandeb Strait and the Black Sea were compounded by climate shocks like El Nino.",
